          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em derived (infinity,1)-category
            or
            %em derived category
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is the setting for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categorical+localization"} (infinity,1)-categorical localization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            at the class of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
            (cf. the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freyd-Mitchell+embedding+theorem"} Freyd-Mitchell embedding theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            says that the derived
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"}
              stable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
          %p
            The derived
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-model+structures"} dg-model structures
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+chain+complexes"} model structures on chain complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretriangulated+dg-category"} pretriangulated dg-category
            = succeed "." do
              %em derived dg-category
          %p
            Like any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            of the derived (infinity,1)-category admits a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            structure. Often in the literature, the term
            %em derived category
            refers to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
          %p
            In what follows, we will describe only the homotopy category. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (infinity,1)-category of chain complexes
            for the full
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
          %p
            Associated to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                which is naturally a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            %li
              %p
                the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+chain+complexes"}> homotopy category of chain complexes
                ”
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%E2%88%9E-category"} stable ∞-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_\infty(\mathcal{A})
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
          %p
            The
            %em derived category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(\mathcal{A}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is equivalently
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} 1-categorical homotopy category
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                with respect to the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categorical homotopy category
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_\infty(\mathcal{A})
          %p
            In either case, this means that under the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Q : Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A}) \to D(\mathcal{A})
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            become true
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(\mathcal{A})
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            with respect to this property.
          %p
            Hence the derived category is an approximation to the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            that give a more accurate approximation. Notably every derived category is a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            and de-suspension operations on its objects – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+of+chain+complexes"} suspension of chain complexes
            – hence its “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}> stability
            ”.
          %h2#history History
          %p
            Derived categories were introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Verdier"} Jean-Louis Verdier
            in his thesis under the supervision of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+Grothendieck"} Alexandre Grothendieck
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+duality"} Serre duality
            to a relative context. See
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Hartshorne"} Hartshorne
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            modulo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homotopy"} chain homotopy
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+chain+complexes"}> homotopy category of chain complexes
            ”).
          %p
            Equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
            with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            by declaring the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            to be the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong quasi-isomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : V \to W
            which induce
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f) : H(V) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H(W)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong derived category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(\mathcal{A})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
              with respect to these weak equivalences.
          %p
            Analogously, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{+,-,b}(\mathcal{A})
            denoting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on the chain complexes bounded above, bounded below, or bounded, respectively (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^{+,-,b}(\mathcal{A}) \hookrightarrow D(\mathcal{A})
          %p for the correspponding full subcategory of the derived category.
          %h2#Properties Equivalent characterizations and constructions
          %p
            There are various ways to construct or express the derived category more explicitly in terms of various special objects or morphisms in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#AsLOcalizationAtNullSystem"} In terms of localization at a null system
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#InTermsOfResolutions"} In terms of resolutions
                \.
          %h3#AsLOcalizationAtNullSystem In terms of localization at a null system
          %p
            The “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+chain+complexes"}> homotopy category of chain complexes
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
            is already a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            with respect to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+system"} null system
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N(\mathcal{A}) \subset K(\mathcal{A})
            %p and analogously
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N^{+,-n,b}(\mathcal{A}) \subset K^{+,-,b}(\mathcal{A})
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
              or on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{+,-,b}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              vanishes in every degree,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet(V) = 0
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet : V_\bullet \to W_\bullet
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              precisely there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distinguished+triangle"} distinguished triangle
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \stackrel{f}{\to} W \to cone(f)
            %p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f) \in N(\mathcal{C})
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The derived category is equivalently the localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
              at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+system"} null system
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{A})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D(\mathcal{A}) \simeq K(\mathcal{A})/N(\mathcal{A})
                    \\,.
          %p
            This perspective is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#KashiwaraSchapira"}> Kashiwara-Schapira, section 13
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Schapira"}> Schapira, section 6.2, 72
            ).
          %h3#InTermsOfResolutions In terms of injective and projective resolutions
          %p
            In the case that the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            has
            %a{:href => "injective%20object#EnoughInjectives"} enough injectives
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "projective%20object#EnoughInjectives"} enough projectives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+sets"} hom sets
            in the derived category may equivalently be obtained as
            = succeed "-classes" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+maps"} chain maps
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolutions"} projective resolutions
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+resolutions"} injective resolutions
            of chain complexes.
          %p
            In view of the existence of the injective and projective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            this is a special case of the general fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            may be obtained by forming homotopy classes of maps in the model category from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolutions"} cofibrant resolutions
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+resolutions"} fibrant resolutions
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TV2007"} Toën, Vaquié
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℐ
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^+(\mathcal{I}_{\mathcal{A}}) \hookrightarrow K^+(\mathcal{A})
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+chain+complexes"} homotopy category of chain complexes
              bounded above on those that are degreewise
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
            %p
              Dually, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^-(\mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{A}}) \hookrightarrow K^-(\mathcal{A})
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+chain+complexes"} homotopy category of chain complexes
              bounded below on those that are degreewise
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+objects"} projective objects
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              has
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/injective%20object#EnoughInjectives"} enough injectives
              then the canonical functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℐ
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K^+(\mathcal{I}_{\mathcal{A}}) \to D^+(\mathcal{A})
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            %p
              Dually, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              has
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/projective%20object#EnoughProjectives"} enough projectives
              then the canonical functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K^-(\mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{A}}) \to D^-(\mathcal{A})
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Schapira"}> Schapira, cor. 7.2.3
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
          %h2#references References
          %p The original reference:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verdier%2C+Jean-Louis"}> Verdier, Jean-Louis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Des Catégories Dérivées des Catégories Abéliennes
                %strong 239
                (1996) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://smf.emath.fr/publications/des-categories-derivees-des-categories-abeliennes"}> doi:10.24033/ast.364
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/issues/AST_1996__239__R1_0"} numdam:AST_1996__239__R1_0
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/AST_1996__239__R1_0.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GelfandManin96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gelfand"}> Sergei Gelfand
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Yuri Manin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Methods+of+homological+algebra"} Methods of homological algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5
          %p
            Systematic discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#KashiwaraSchapira
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
              (2006)
          %p and, similarly, in section 7 of
          %ul#Schapira
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"}> Pierre Schapira
              ,
              %em Categories and homological algebra
              (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~schapira/lectnotes/HomAl.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/Pierre_Schapira___Categories_and_Homological_Algebra"} archive.org
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://perso.imj-prg.fr/pierre-schapira/wp-content/uploads/schapira-pub/lectnotes/HomAl.pdf"} newer version(pdf)
          %p
            For the model-category version of this story for an arbitrary ringed site, including details about the tensor, internal hom, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_!
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^*
          %ul
            %li#TV2007
              Bertrand Toën, Michel Vaquié,
              %em Algebraization of complex analytic varieties and derived categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0703555v1"}> arXiv:math/0703555v1
              )
          %p A detailed treatment of derived categories (including of DG modules over DG rings), with applications to noncommutative algebra, is in the book
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Yekutieli"}> Amnon Yekutieli
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Derived Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108292825"} doi:10.1017/9781108292825
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09640"} arXiv:1610.09640
          %p A pedagogical introduction:
          %ul
            %li
              R. P. Thomas,
              %em Derived categories for the working mathematician
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AG/0001045"}> arXiv:math.AG/0001045
              )
          %p A good survey of the more general topic of derived categories is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Keller"}> Bernhard Keller
              ,
              %em Derived categories and their uses
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.google.de/url?sa=t&source=web&ct=res&cd=6&ved=0CC8QFjAF&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.math.jussieu.fr%2F~keller%2Fpubl%2Fdcu.ps&rct=j&q=derived+category&ei=Ib76SsSdAsjb-QaAw7moDw&usg=AFQjCNGIgXLHlprAoR70bGLWQmyKGHDjTQ"}> ps
              )
          %p See in particular also the list of references given there.
          %p Other lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li
              Theo Bühler,
              %em An introduction to the derived category
              (
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/intro-derived.PDF"}> pdf
              ).
          %p
            and for applications to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franco+Rota"}> Franco Rota
              ,
              %em An introduction to the derived category of coherent sheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "https://drive.google.com/file/d/12fhshN_lFOi54pjBdjVEPzUb1XBxz-TW/view"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            For a discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            and in particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-categories
            see
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/DAG-I.pdf#page=53"} section 13, p. 53
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+%E2%88%9E-Categories"} Stable ∞-Categories
          %p
            On applications of derived categories in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"}> Dmitri Orlov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Derived categories of coherent sheaves and equivalences between them
                %a{:href => "http://www.mi.ras.ru/~orlov/papers/Uspekhi2003.pdf"} English translation (PDF)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aleksei+Bondal"}> Aleksei Bondal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"} Dmitri Orlov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.mi.ras.ru/~orlov/papers/Compositio2001.pdf"} Reconstruction of a variety from the derived category and groups of autoequivalences
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bondal-Orlov+reconstruction+theorem"} Bondal-Orlov reconstruction theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Huybrechts"}> Daniel Huybrechts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fourier-Mukai Transforms in Algebraic Geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Dolgachev"}> Igor Dolgachev
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~idolga/derived9.pdf"}
                    %em Derived categories
            %li
              %p
                Andrei Caldararu,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Derived categories of coherent sheaves: a skimming
                %em Algebraic Geometry: Presentations by Young Researchers
                in Snowbird, Utah, July 2004 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0501094"}> arXiv:math/0501094
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of rings being encoded in the respective derived categories:
          %ul
            %li#DuggerShipley04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              = succeed "," do
                %em K-theory and derived equivalences
              %strong 124
              3 (2004) 587-617 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0209084"}> arXiv:math/0209084
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/duke-mathematical-journal/volume-124/issue-3/K-theory-and-derived-equivalences/10.1215/S0012-7094-04-12435-2.short"} doi:10.1215/S0012-7094-04-12435-2
        .revisedby
